---
export const prerender = true;
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="DMCA Policy | Furry Fediverse">
    <main class="p-2 md:p-5 lg:px-60 2xl:px-80">
        <div class="flex flex-col">
            <div
                class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm bg-[#31dcb2] px-4 py-2 rounded-md"
            >
                <a href="/" class="text-[#12384b] font-semibold">Home</a>
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[#12384b]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
                </svg>
                <span class="text-[#12384b] font-semibold">Legal</span>
                <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-[#12384b]" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
                    <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 5l7 7-7 7"></path>
                </svg>
                <span class="text-[#12384b] font-semibold">DMCA Policy</span>
            </div>

            <div class="py-6 max-w-4xl">
                <h1 class="font-bold text-2xl text-white">DMCA / Copyright Infringement Policy</h1>
                <p class="text-white/50 text-sm mt-1">Based on CYBERFURZ LLC policy</p>

                <div class="mt-6 bg-white/5 rounded-xl p-6 border border-white/10 space-y-4 text-white/80 leading-relaxed">
                    <p>
                        The Digital Millennium Copyright Act (DMCA), including Title 17 U.S. Code
                        section 512, sets out how online service providers must handle copyright
                        infringement notices.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        None of this material should be construed as legal advice. If you need legal
                        guidance, contact a lawyer licensed in your jurisdiction.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Notification of copyright infringement</h2>
                    <p>
                        If you believe content on our services infringes your copyright, submit a
                        notice by email to
                        <a href="mailto:dmca@cyberfurz.org" class="text-[#31dcb2] hover:underline">dmca@cyberfurz.org</a>
                        or by physical mail to:
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        CYBERFURZ LLC<br />
                        1108 East Main St, Ste 906 #3268<br />
                        Richmond, Virginia 23219, United States
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Notices should include: your signature, identification of the copyrighted
                        work, specific URL(s) of allegedly infringing material, contact information,
                        a good-faith statement of unauthorized use, and a perjury statement that the
                        notice is accurate and authorized.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Takedown process</h2>
                    <p>
                        Upon receiving a valid notice, we may disable access to allegedly infringing
                        material and forward the notice to the account owner. Where media takedown is
                        not possible, the related post may be removed.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Users receiving a notice may accept the allegation, decline it without filing
                        a counter-notification, or file a counter-notification. Re-uploading content
                        before process completion may lead to account restriction.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Counter-notification</h2>
                    <p>
                        A counter-notification under 17 U.S.C. section 512(g)(3) may be submitted if
                        you believe content was removed due to mistake or misidentification.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Counter-notifications should include: your signature, relevant URL, a
                        good-faith perjury statement, your name/address/phone, consent to proper
                        court jurisdiction, and acceptance of service of process.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        Filing a counter-notification may involve legal risk. Consider consulting
                        qualified legal counsel first.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Restoration process</h2>
                    <p>
                        If a valid counter-notification is received, it is forwarded to the original
                        notifier. If no court action is reported in the required window, access may
                        be restored in accordance with statutory timelines.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Repeat offenders</h2>
                    <p>
                        Accounts of repeat copyright infringers may be disabled. We reserve discretion
                        to define and enforce repeat offender handling and to address abuse of DMCA
                        processes.
                    </p>

                    <h2 class="font-bold text-xl text-white">Acknowledgements and license</h2>
                    <p>
                        This policy is based on the CYBERFURZ LLC DMCA policy,
                        PawbSocial DMCA policy, and the Dreamwidth DMCA policy.
                    </p>
                    <p>
                        The DMCA policy text is available for reuse under the
                        Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 2.5 license.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </main>
</Layout>
